This project changes the decision head and the final three encoder layers
of the typed-decisions checkpoint through supervised Doom-specific training.
It is an independent experiment, not an official Laya or Jev release.

ViZDoom, FreeDoom and third-party Python dependencies are installed separately
and retain their own licenses. No Doom/FreeDoom WAD or ViZDoom binary is included
in the source repository or model bundle. Original third-party Telegram text
and the supplied Jev instructions are excluded from the publication set.
